---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR, AUTHOR_URL } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why this log exists and what goes in it."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    This is a working log. I build things — tools, sites, systems — and this is
    where I write down how, while it's still happening rather than after it's
    safely finished.
  </p>

  <p>
    Finished work gets a case study: tidy, sequenced, with the wrong turns
    quietly removed. That's a useful artifact and a dishonest record. The
    interesting part of building is the part that gets edited out — the
    decision made on partial information, the approach abandoned in week two,
    the constraint nobody saw coming. So that's what goes here.
  </p>

  <h2>What to expect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Posts are dated and written as the work happens.</li>
    <li>Each post belongs to a <a href="/projects/">project</a>, so any build can be read start to now.</li>
    <li>Dead ends stay in. A reversed decision is kept, not deleted.</li>
    <li>No schedule. Posts appear when there's something worth reporting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who's writing</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={AUTHOR_URL}>{AUTHOR}</a> — product designer. My work,
    background, and case studies live at <a href={AUTHOR_URL}>catherinehicks.com</a>.
  </p>

  <p>You can follow along by <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
